<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p><strong>Version 1.0, dated 16 October 2026.</strong> This notice explains what personal data AcxiomCRM collects, why it is used, and the rights available to you. It is aligned with the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 of India (DPDPA). This page is not legal advice. Updates are listed at the end with the version date.</p>

<h2>1. Who we are</h2>
<p>AcxiomCRM, 123 Business Street, Mumbai, Maharashtra, India. Phone: <a href="tel:+911234567890">+91 12345 67890</a>. Email: <a href="mailto:support@example.in">support@example.in</a>. Working hours: Monday to Friday, 9:00 to 18:00 IST.</p>
<p>Grievance Officer: Grievance Officer, AcxiomCRM, at the address above, email <a href="mailto:support@example.in">support@example.in</a>. Grievances are acknowledged and resolved within 30 days.</p>

<h2>2. Data we collect (minimum only)</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Account data: full name, email address, role assignment, sign-in records (timestamps, failed attempt counts, lockout state).</li>
    <li>CRM records entered by authorised users: customer, lead, opportunity, follow-up and activity details (names, contact details, notes, dates, outcomes).</li>
    <li>Technical logs: IP address, timestamps, and audit events needed for security and operation.</li>
    <li>Support messages sent to us, and cookie consent choices (accepted or rejected, with timestamp).</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not collect Aadhaar numbers, biometric data, financial account numbers, passwords in readable form, Precise location, or any other data beyond what is listed above. Optional form fields are marked as optional.</p>

<h2>3. Purpose and purpose limitation</h2>
<p>Personal data is used only for the purpose stated at collection: providing user accounts and sign-in, operating the CRM records assigned to each role, protecting the service against misuse, and responding to support requests. Data is never reused for an incompatible purpose such as marketing without fresh consent.</p>

<h2>4. Consent and withdrawal</h2>
<p>Where consent is the basis (account registration, cookie preferences, optional contact), it is free, specific and informed. Consent checkboxes are never pre-ticked. Consent can be withdrawn at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:support@example.in">support@example.in</a> or, for cookies, by choosing Cookie Preferences in the footer. Withdrawal does not affect processing already completed. Staff-entered CRM records are processed for legitimate business purposes and are managed by the organisation administrator.</p>

<h2>5. Retention</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Account data: kept while the account is active, then deleted within 90 days of verified deletion requests (backups expire on a rolling 30 day cycle).</li>
    <li>Audit and security logs: kept 1 to 3 years for security and accountability, then deleted.</li>
    <li>Support messages: kept up to 1 year after resolution.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. Your rights</h2>
<p>You may request access to your data, correction of inaccuracies, erasure where the law permits, and nomination of another person to exercise rights on your behalf. You may raise grievances with the Grievance Officer above, and then with the Data Protection Board of India under the DPDPA process. Requests are answered within 30 days.</p>

<h2>7. Security</h2>
<p>Passwords are stored only as one-way hashes, never in readable form. Access follows role-based permissions with account lockout after repeated failed sign-ins. The service uses HTTPS in production, append-only audit logging, and access-controlled hosting. Suspected breaches are assessed promptly, affected users are notified as the law requires, and regulators are informed where applicable.</p>

<h2>8. Children</h2>
<p>AcxiomCRM is a business tool. We do not knowingly collect data of persons under 18. Accounts found to belong to children are suspended pending guardian consent or deleted.</p>

<h2>9. Processors and hosting region</h2>
<p>Data is hosted where the organisation deploys this application, in the India region by default for production use. Self-hosted deployments keep data with the deploying organisation. No analytics, advertising, chat widget, or social media tracker is enabled by default. If the organisation enables an optional processor (for example email delivery), only the minimum data needed is shared under a purpose-limited arrangement. A processor table is maintained by the administrator and reviewed quarterly.</p>

<h2>10. Updates</h2>
<p>Material changes are announced on this page with a new version date before they take effect.</p>
<p>Version history: 1.0 (16 October 2026): first published version.</p>
